{"repositoryId":1349357252,"availability":"available","full":"UmarSiddiqui/heymate","name":"heymate","description":"The AI buddy that lives in your Mac's notch. Push-to-talk, sees your screen, answers out loud, and runs Claude Code / Codex / OpenCode agents on the subscription you already have. Free, open source, native SwiftUI.","category":"Productivity","language":"Swift","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-08-28T08:11:13Z","updated":"2026-10-12T11:39:10Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://getheymate.vercel.app","topics":["ai-agents","ai-assistant","claude","claude-code","codex","coding-agent","llm","local-first","macbook-notch","macos","macos-app","mcp","notch","open-source","opencode","productivity","push-to-talk","swift","swiftui","voice-assistant"],"demo":"https://getheymate.vercel.app/#demo","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:00.246Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:00.246Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:00.246Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T11:46:00.246Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ask how to do something in a desktop app or website. HeyMate points to the next step, explains it out loud, and waits while you try it. Currently available for macOS.","The open-source alternative to HeyClicky. Bring your own AI: your existing Claude, ChatGPT (Codex), or OpenCode subscription does the work. HeyMate is free and MIT licensed; we do not meter your model use. Provider limits and optional paid connectors still apply.","Hold ⌃ ⌥, ask about anything on screen, let go. Illustrated example: ask \"why is my Mac so slow?\" and get a spoken answer with a pointer."],"features":["Help with desktop apps and websites. Spoken explanations and a cursor that points at the control being discussed. Screen context is captured during active interactions that need it, including each step of a walkthrough.","Bring your own AI. Sign in through the official Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode CLI with the subscription or models you already pay for. HeyMate adds no subscription fee and does not meter your model use. Provider…","Keep control of coding work. Agents show a read-only plan before execution. Approved jobs get workspace snapshots for undo; external actions are subject to their tool's approval policy. Undo cannot reverse a sent…","Folds into the camera housing and opens on hover into Home, Apps, and Agents. Macs without a notch get a top-center pill. There is no dock icon and no menu-bar clutter.","Micro-apps for the space you never used: File Shelf with AirDrop, focus timers, Clipboard history, Now Playing with album art, Downloads, Camera Mirror, Volume and Brightness HUDs, Bluetooth devices, Battery, Next…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UmarSiddiqui/heymate/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"aac3fabcfa7ed6f14f484edcf1a8e820a1275276cccb2eb373afef4c1d490bb8","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:00.374Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:00.374Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ask how to do something in a desktop app or website. HeyMate points to the next step, explains it out loud, and waits while you try it. Currently available for macOS.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UmarSiddiqui/heymate/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Provider limits and optional paid connectors still apply.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UmarSiddiqui/heymate/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Sign in through the official Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode CLI with the subscription or models you already pay for.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UmarSiddiqui/heymate/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign in through the official Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode CLI with the subscription or models you already pay for.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/UmarSiddiqui/heymate/blob/main/README.